Scope and third-party content

The licence above covers this repository's own content: the scripts under
scripts/ (dotswitch, dotdoctor, fork-check, shell-rebuild, shell-restart and
the overlay tooling), the profile configuration under profiles/, shared/ and
apps/, the systemd units, and home/.

It does not cover, and cannot relicense, the following:

  * The embedded upstream clones listed in profiles/UPSTREAM.md. They are
    excluded from this repository by .gitignore precisely because they carry
    their own history and their own terms; the manifest records where each one
    came from and at which commit. They remain under their upstream licences.

  * The Quickshell fork at DaveLewis360/shell, which is a separate repository
    and stays under GPL-3.0, inherited from caelestia-dots/shell.

  * Any configuration here that is adapted from an upstream project rather than
    written for this repository. Where that is the case, that project's terms
    apply to the adapted parts. Note that caelestia-dots/hyprland and
    caelestia-dots/caelestia declare no licence at all, so no redistribution
    permission can be assumed for material taken from them — treat anything
    derived from those as unlicensed upstream content rather than as covered by
    the MIT grant above.
